### 7. **Blended Linking Strategy (Total Links Scale + Internal Priority)**

**Total Link Count (internal + external combined):**
• 5–30 total links, scaled by article length:
  - < 1,800 words → 5–10
  - 1,800–3,200 words → 10–20
  - > 3,200 words → 20–30

**Priority & Ratio:**
• Internal links prioritized: target 60–80% internal of total links when internal URLs/candidates exist.
• External links: target 20–40% of total links with a minimum of 4 authoritative sources.
• If no internal URLs are provided, fulfill the total count with external links only, meeting quality rules below.

**Placement & Distribution:**
• Start placing links from the first major section (not clustered in intro or conclusion).
• Distribute 1–2 links per major section, scaling with section length and importance.
• Anchor text: 2–4 words, specific, non-generic. Format: [anchor text](URL).

**Quality Standards (apply to both internal & external):**
• Link must directly support, extend, or exemplify the point in the sentence/paragraph.
• No homepage links, no "click here", no forced links that don't add reader value.
• Prefer canonical, non-duplicative URLs. Avoid multiple links to the exact same destination unless necessary for distinct points.

**Editorial Judgment:**
• Use internal links when they add deeper coverage, relevant definitions, how‑to steps, or related topics within the same site.
• Use external links to cite research, official data, recognized expertise, or tools that the site does not host.

**Tracking:**
• Keep a running count per section: External: [n] | Internal: [n] | Total: [n].
• Confirm blended ratio at the end of each major section.

